summary:
Plan annotations and plan dimensions already do the same thing in both apps. Annotations differ only by TV Toolbar 1.1.0, which hands the dimension colour to the Colour Palette (TV v2.126.0) and so waits for the 54 port. Dimensions differ only structurally: VV split out ConfigState and EditorPreview; TV copied those two files but never wired them, so TV now runs two copies of the config and its Layout Editor MarkupBridge reads defaults from a ConfigState that is never loaded. VV's split is the target and the fix belongs on TV's side. The swarm must not copy TV's PlanDimensions Data or Editor onto VV.

Projected linework (folder 50) is where most of the work is. 11 of 25 shared files have no real code difference, and VV already has owner tags, linetype annotation, the content stamp and ForgetCollections. What VV lacks is every TV linework change since v2.37.0:
- the 3D-matching rules (FlushJoins, SeamsOcclude, LineworkFirst), signed off in TV, with the v2.159.0 flush tolerance;
- door pose (v2.42.0 and v2.48.1), storeys (v2.105.0) and the hide-swings hit test (v2.140.0);
- nested LineworkModifier owners (20-Sep, which has no TV devlog entry);
- the design-phase seams.

That means 3 TV-only modules (DoorPose, FlushJoins, Storeys) plus 12 changed files and the config. One constraint is critical. DoorPose imports TV door module 1.9.0 exports and FindDoorGroups, which VV does not have, and Projector 1.5.0 calls DoorPose on every collection. So VV's 25 door module must be upgraded first, keeping VV's Video Studio exports, or the whole drawing module graph fails to link. Persistence keeps VV's folder-id resolution (DIV-4). No worker or server change is needed. The new BuildToken forces a one-off re-bake of every VV project.

The depth fog (TV 49, 8 files) should go into VV folder 49 under the same number. Its pure modules carry over unchanged. Three things must be adapted:
- one fog call inside VV's ComposerPreset RenderFrame, which also covers VV thumbnails, plus an export hook (DIV-1);
- a depth-only section-cap render from VV's CrossSectionView (DIV-2);
- the Dev row, which needs DevRowShell.

VV's 29 FogPlaneSystem is a separate 3D-view feature, switched off in drawings, and does not conflict with the depth fog.

Two related gaps sit in other slices: the orthographic fat-line depth bias (15) and the supersampler premultiplied clamp (05). Several records are wrong. The ledger marks the dimension split as closed, files the Lantern Designer items as TV work, and has no rows for any TV linework change since v2.37.0. TV's back-port markers are stale, the TV v2.159.0 devlog wrongly says VV has FlushJoins, and the two apps use clashing version numbers for the same files.
